.SH HISTORY
.IX Header "HISTORY"
Until OpenSSL 1.1.0, by default (unless \fBX509_V_FLAG_TRUSTED_FIRST\fR was set), when building a
certificate chain, if the first certificate chain found was not trusted,
OpenSSL would attempt to replace untrusted certificates supplied by the peer
with certificates from the trust store to see if an alternative chain can be
found that is trusted.
Since OpenSSL 1.1.0 version, the \fBX509_V_FLAG_TRUSTED_FIRST\fR is set by default.
.PP
The \fBX509_V_FLAG_NO_ALT_CHAINS\fR flag was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
The flag \fBX509_V_FLAG_CB_ISSUER_CHECK\fR was deprecated in OpenSSL 1.1.0
and has no effect.
.PP
The function \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_add0_policy()\fR was historically documented as
enabling policy checking however the implementation has never done this.
The documentation was changed to align with the implementation.
.PP
The \fBX509_VERIFY_PARAM_get_purpose()\fR function was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
